WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.552
Albert Chamillard

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.192
geometric pen drawings

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.194
on old ledgers

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:05.995
An Abakcus gallery

00:00:05.807 --> 00:00:06.679
of a Tucson

00:00:06.491 --> 00:00:07.705
artist's isometric

00:00:07.517 --> 00:00:08.165
cubes

00:00:08.271 --> 00:00:09.533
cylinders and ribbons

00:00:09.344 --> 00:00:10.335
drawn on vintage

00:00:10.146 --> 00:00:11.042
ledger paper

00:00:11.078 --> 00:00:12.304
using only three

00:00:12.116 --> 00:00:13.235
hatching densities

00:00:13.047 --> 00:00:13.955
from one pen

00:00:14.132 --> 00:00:15.287
with an interactive

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:16.184
three-tone cube

00:00:16.702 --> 00:00:18.011
Because an isometric

00:00:17.822 --> 00:00:19.225
cube shows exactly

00:00:19.037 --> 00:00:20.746
three face orientations

00:00:20.947 --> 00:00:21.878
three tones are

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:22.480
enough to make

00:00:22.292 --> 00:00:23.199
shapes read as

00:00:23.011 --> 00:00:23.989
solid with no

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:24.579
outlines

00:00:24.674 --> 00:00:25.687
and some cubes

00:00:25.499 --> 00:00:26.525
flip inside out

00:00:26.336 --> 00:00:27.303
like the Penrose

00:00:27.115 --> 00:00:27.869
triangle

00:00:28.406 --> 00:00:29.597
18 drawings in

00:00:29.408 --> 00:00:31.495
this gallery 30-50 hours

00:00:31.307 --> 00:00:32.356
for a full-size

00:00:32.168 --> 00:00:33.382
sheet 3 tones

00:00:33.512 --> 00:00:34.361
all from one

00:00:34.172 --> 00:00:34.726
pen

00:00:35.262 --> 00:00:36.276
Full story on

00:00:36.087 --> 00:00:36.983
the dashboard
